cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper."
title: "What de-identified timestamps support in MIMIC-IV and eICU-CRD"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and aggregate outputs for an empirical audit of the
  de-identified timestamps of MIMIC-IV v3.1 and eICU-CRD v2.0. The checks
  test whether calendar position (weekday, season), cross-patient
  concurrency, time of day and timestamp precision are preserved, and
  determine the clock reference of the eICU-CRD clock fields with a
  laboratory-routine anchor, a physiological (heart-rate and
  respiratory-rate) anchor and an administrative (discharge-time) anchor
  against MIMIC-IV local time. A worked example repeats a published
  eICU-CRD analysis of heart-rate peak time and in-hospital mortality on
  the recorded clock and in local time. A synthetic-data generator with
  planted effects is included for testing. No record-level data or
  eICU-CRD hospital identifiers are included.
